{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"213","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A. Game"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Furik and Rubik love playing computer games. Furik has recently found a new game that greatly interested Rubik. The game consists of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" parts and to complete each part a player may probably need to complete some other ones. We know that the game can be fully completed, that is, its parts do not form cyclic dependencies. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Rubik has "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"3"},{"kind":"text","text":" computers, on which he can play this game. All computers are located in different houses. Besides, it has turned out that each part of the game can be completed only on one of these computers. Let's number the computers with integers from "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"3"},{"kind":"text","text":". Rubik can perform the following actions: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Complete some part of the game on some computer. Rubik spends exactly "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" hour on completing any part on any computer. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Move from the 1-st computer to the 2-nd one. Rubik spends exactly "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" hour on that. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Move from the 1-st computer to the 3-rd one. Rubik spends exactly "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2"},{"kind":"text","text":" hours on that. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Move from the 2-nd computer to the 1-st one. Rubik spends exactly "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2"},{"kind":"text","text":" hours on that. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Move from the 2-nd computer to the 3-rd one. Rubik spends exactly "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" hour on that. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Move from the 3-rd computer to the 1-st one. Rubik spends exactly "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" hour on that. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Move from the 3-rd computer to the 2-nd one. Rubik spends exactly "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2"},{"kind":"text","text":" hours on that. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Help Rubik to find the minimum number of hours he will need to complete all parts of the game. Initially Rubik can be located at the computer he considers necessary. "}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(1 ≤ n ≤ 200)"},{"kind":"text","text":" — the number of game parts. The next line contains "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" integers, the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th integer — "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ci"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(1 ≤ ci ≤ 3)"},{"kind":"text","text":" represents the number of the computer, on which you can complete the game part number "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Next "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" lines contain descriptions of game parts. The "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th line first contains integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ki"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(0 ≤ ki ≤ n - 1)"},{"kind":"text","text":", then "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ki"},{"kind":"text","text":" distinct integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ai, j"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(1 ≤ ai, j ≤ n; ai, j ≠ i)"},{"kind":"text","text":" — the numbers of parts to complete before part "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Numbers on all lines are separated by single spaces. You can assume that the parts of the game are numbered from 1 to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" in some way. It is guaranteed that there are no cyclic dependencies between the parts of the game."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"On a single line print the answer to the problem."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"1\n1\n0\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"1\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"5\n2 2 1 1 3\n1 5\n2 5 1\n2 5 4\n1 5\n0\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"7\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note to the second sample: before the beginning of the game the best strategy is to stand by the third computer. First we complete part 5. Then we go to the 1-st computer and complete parts 3 and 4. Then we go to the 2-nd computer and complete parts 1 and 2. In total we get 1+1+2+1+2, which equals 7 hours."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"A","problemCode":"213A","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/213/problem/A"}